  <prompt>Make the To Do composite score's urgency component count calendar days (as the due label already does) and make every board use that one function.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE front-end developer. One scorer, no copies.</role>
  <goal>computeTodoScore's urgency and computeDueLabel agree for every due date; no other copy of the urgency or score computation exists; boards re-rank once.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>D-29 (spec section 9): To Do composite score to calendar days, one shared function (boards re-rank once). In Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/utils/todoScoring.ts, computeDueDateUrgencyRaw uses Math.ceil over a millisecond difference (time-of-day dependent), while computeDueLabel compares local-midnight calendar days. C-10 (task 084, merged) already removed one drifted copy in useKanbanColumns; task 081 (#1309) touches SmartTodo code and must merge first to avoid conflicts.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/utils/todoScoring.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/__tests__/todoScoring.kanbanParity.tz.test.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/hooks/useKanbanColumns.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-29): the urgency raw score uses the same calendar-day difference as computeDueLabel (local midnight to local midnight, Math.round for DST); tier thresholds and weights are unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-29): exactly one implementation: grep src/ for any other copy of the urgency or composite computation (including src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/hooks/useKanbanColumns.ts) and make it call the shared function.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: no change to colour tiers or labels.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>To Do scoring</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/tasks/084-todo-scorer-own-pr.poml</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code.</step>
    <step order="1">Extract one calendar-day difference helper used by both computeDueLabel and the urgency score.</step>
    <step order="2">Find and remove any other copy.</step>
    <step order="3">Tests: a due date today at 23:00 and tomorrow at 01:00 score by calendar day; label and urgency agree across a DST change.</step>
    <step order="4">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="5">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Board re-rank">
      <steps>
        <step>Open Smart To Do with To Dos due today, tomorrow and overdue</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Order and column placement match the due labels.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode compliance per ADR-021">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Unchanged colours via tokens.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build and test the SmartTodo package</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/utils/todoScoring.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given due dates at different times of day on the same calendar day, when scored, then their urgency components are equal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given any due date, when computeDueLabel and the urgency score are computed, then they place it in the same tier.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: grep finds no second implementation of the urgency or composite computation in src/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests cover the stated contract and the DST case; the package builds.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-63; D-29.</notes>

  <completion>COMPLETED 2026-10-09: PR #1525 merged into docs/ontology-platform-design (ee9617058) after independent review (approved, no F-class). One shared function computeTodoScoreBreakdown/todoUrgencyRaw in Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/dateLocal.ts on calendar days (daysBetweenLocalMidnight + dueUrgencyForDays); five old copies removed or delegated; New_York DST tests (9/12 fail on the old math). Deviation: placed in ui-components (TodoDetail cannot import SmartTodo.Components); kanbanParity test left unchanged (covered by the new NY test). Built bundles carry the old math until redeployed. D-106 items: F-30..F-32, F-40.</completion>

